161:🪞 **F-2649-1 — F-2498-1’S DUPLICATE CHECK MET ITS HARDEST CASE AND PASSED ONLY BECAUSE I DIFFED: THE SAME BRANCH PRODUCED TWO DRAINS WITH *OPPOSITE* GZ-01 VERDICTS, AND A `NOT PLAYER-VISIBLE` DISMISSAL FOR IT WAS ALREADY STANDING (measured s2649).** The gazette sweep offered `532a7ffb5` — the attended drain of `sol/map-art-campaign-2`. A dismissal naming that exact branch was already in `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md`, filed by s2643, whose own words are *"That drain is EVIDENCE ONLY ... no map advanced"*. Every cheap key agrees they are the same story: same branch, same campaign, same artist, same master family, adjacent days. 📊 **ONLY THE DIFF SEPARATES THEM, AND IT SEPARATES THEM COMPLETELY: s2643’s subject is run 1 — `49` files, EVERY ONE under `artifacts/`, engine hash unmoved. Mine is run 2 — `675` files, of which the player-path set is `src/world/Water.ts`, `src/world/Terrain3dClaimPilot.ts` and the Mare dome landmark pack (`air-pad-dome.glb` + its contract and blend). One landed NOTHING a rider can see; the other re-applies the E5 shared sea, lifts the Relay Valley landmark bodies and gives two domes their drums.** ⓘ **The candidate is a MERGE, so `git show --stat` is EMPTY and the file list had to be asked as a diff against its FIRST PARENT — the same trap s2612 and s2623 each record.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing was lost, NOT a false green, and no verdict anywhere was wrong — I filed the item and the near-duplicate never reached the owner.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is the DIRECTION and the fact that the resemblance is not superficial: F-1600-1 prices duplicate news to the owner as WORSE than doing nothing, and every prior instance in this chain was two items that merely LOOKED alike (s2498’s nine contracts, s2611’s town cast, s2618’s Baron facings, s2623’s open-maps landing). **Here the two share a BRANCH NAME, which is the strongest resemblance this factory can produce short of a real duplicate — and the standing item is a DISMISSAL, so the trap is not "file it twice" but "conclude it was already judged not-news and file nothing at all".** A fire that read the standing paragraph and stopped would have dropped the campaign’s only player-visible landing on the floor, and the sweep would have kept re-offering it forever. ➡️ **THEREFORE, WIDENING F-2498-1 RATHER THAN RESTATING IT: a standing item that names your candidate’s BRANCH is not evidence your candidate was judged — a branch is a CONTAINER that emits many drains, and consecutive runs of one campaign routinely differ in kind (evidence-only, then code). Diff the two COMMITS, never compare their branches, their headlines or their masters; and when the standing item is a DISMISSAL, read what it actually dismissed — s2643’s says EVIDENCE ONLY in its own words, which is what settled it in one read.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: "is this candidate the same story as a standing item?" is a JUDGEMENT over prose, so a red would fire on every legitimate second item about a long-running thread and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate) — exactly the restraint F-2498-1 itself took. The cure is the sentence you are reading, at the site.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS for this chain: every prior duplicate scare asked whether two ITEMS were the same. This one asks whether two COMMITS ON ONE BRANCH are the same WORK — and the answer is that a branch identity carries no verdict at all. When your candidate resembles something already judged, ask what the standing judgement was ABOUT, not what it was NAMED AFTER.**
