e been ZERO fs-writes in `114.0` min across ALL `493,895` files of its scratchpad (22 worktrees) — the newest file anywhere beneath it IS phase D's own `run-queue.sh`. §2A: *a RESIDENT attended pid with zero fs-writes >30 min = IDLE, not live-driving*.** ⓘ **Nor did the output land elsewhere: `ls -d artifacts/gauntlet-heat14*` → *"no matches found"* and `git ls-files 'artifacts/gauntlet-heat14*'` → EMPTY, so there is no heat-14 output on main either, tracked or untracked.** ⏱️ **Quietness was resolved by the newest mtime of an actual FILE and in EPOCH MILLISECONDS ON BOTH SIDES (F-2607-1 + F-2567-1). ⚠️ Note the trap this arena sets: its tree ROOT mtime reads the SAME instant as its newest file, so root and file agree here — a coincidence of the tree never having been written since creation, and it must NOT be read as vindicating the root as a work signal.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY STATED HONESTLY AND DELIBERATELY NOT INFLATED: realised cost ZERO, nothing is lost, nothing is broken, NOT a false green, and NO VERDICT ANYWHERE WAS WRONG. s2614's instruction carried a SECOND, MEASURABLE ARM — *"do not skip it once the tree is quiet — and resolve quietness by the newest mtime of an actual FILE"* — and that arm is the ONLY reason this was resolvable in one command; I took the sweep rather than waiting for a landing.** 🎯 **What earns it a row is the DIRECTION of the FIRST arm: keyed on the LANDING alone the deferral is PERMANENT, because nothing is running that could land. And the belief costs in the other direction too — F-2495-1 makes in-flight arena evidence REPORT-ONLY, so a fire that believes an arena is riding treats 18 untracked controllers as untouchable in-flight work rather than asking whether they are DURABLE at all, and controllers are precisely what F-2487-1 says EARNS salvage.** 📜 **THE PRECEDENT IS NAMED AND EXACT: Mistake #16 — *"lock/handoff messages announce INTENT; only a merge commit + review file is a completion … NEVER by grepping commit MESSAGES, which match every announcement of the thing."* That rule is written for MERGES; this is the same defect on a HEAT LAUNCH, where *"operator launched"* is the announcement and the arena's own contents are the artifact.** 🚫 **NO GUARD, and the restraint is INHERITED rather than re-argued: an arena that is set up and idle is a LAWFUL state — the owner may ride it later, and the standing CODEX-WALL routes implementation to the attended session — so a red on *"a registered arena holds no ride output"* would fire during ordinary correct operation and be excused into uselessness inside a week (F-1460-1, the `cross-engine` fate), which is the same restraint F-2357-1, F-2389-1, F-2484-1, F-2485-1, F-2487-1, F-2488-1, F-2489-1 and F-2495-1 all took for this very sweep. The cure is the sentence you are reading.** 💡 **REUSABLE, and it is a NEW AXIS after *how WIDE is the selector* (F-2358-1), *which TREE* (F-2484-1), *a registry is not a census* (F-2485-1), *entries vs files* (F-2490-1), *which CLOCK* (F-2567-1) and *an mtime records a DELETION too* (F-2607-1): every one of those interrogates a MEASUREMENT. **THIS ONE INTERROGATES A PREMISE THAT WAS NEVER A MEASUREMENT AT ALL** — an announcement of intent, promoted to an observed event, and then used to GATE owed work. When a handoff defers work until an external event happens, ask what ARTIFACT would prove it happened and measure THAT: an announcement is not an occurrence, and a gate keyed on an announcement carries no expiry.
