731:🧵✅ **sprite-cell-manifests READY-FOR-GATES → ✅ SHIPPED eeae358aa (drained; see the SHIPPED row above) on `feat/sprite-cell-manifests` (Claude Opus 5 on scratch `wt-cells`, 2026-09-06) — THE 241 CELL-URL MODULES ARE GONE, AND `eager: true` WAS THE WHOLE CURE.** Measured first, as the master ordered: Vite's `?url` glob with `{ eager: true }` inlines every hashed cell URL into the importing chunk, so no manifest file, plugin or build step was needed — the glob IS the manifest and cannot drift from `assets/processed/`. e1 release build: 921 → 135 JS chunks, 785 → 0 per-cell URL modules (95,433 B of them), total JS 5,648,482 → 5,366,611 B, and the ENTRY chunk got SMALLER (1,143,893 → 1,135,958 B) because 786 dynamic-import call sites cost more than the strings they fetched. Deploy's own instrument, both projects: JS responses in the first-town window 205/206 → 32, cell-URL modules 172/173 → 0 (20,720/20,843 B), JS families 51 → 32; NO PNG family left the window and two arrived that used to miss it (`char-hero-sheet-attack8/work8.png`, both already pinned). Timings, 3 runs per project per arm: at 100 ms RTT with bandwidth free the town is READY 20% sooner (1,510 → 1,209 ms desktop, 1,512 → 1,204 ms mobile); at 8 Mbps/100 ms it is fully SETTLED ~1.2-1.5 s sooner (34,191 → 33,035 ms desktop, 34,882 → 33,086 ms mobile) with 637 → 360 requests, while `ready` itself lands ~250 ms LATER because that signal is GLTF-only (F-BUDGET-4) and the sheets now compete for the pipe earlier — the honest limit, recorded not hidden. Guard `sprite-cell-url-inlining` (3 tests, proven to bite) pins both globs eager AND builds a real Vite fixture proving eager emits zero per-cell modules while lazy emits one each, and that the inlined table equals the file set with no URL the build did not emit. asset-diet gains a count-and-cell-set assertion; the family allowlist carries a dated reason. Evidence `artifacts/sprite-cell-manifests/`. Engine hash `1517199d639fc0326cc020487ce4ad7e9803a4357e8fa930bc2cf6b47c193b1c` — THE DRAIN PINS IT. GATE: tsc clean; dev + `GR_RELEASE=e1` builds green; `first-town-request-families` 4/4, new guard 3/3, `deploy-budget` 12/12, `no-emdash`+`glob-fallback`+`character-direction` green; e2e `asset-diet` 13/14 (the 0.16-vs-0.15 screenshot red is the environmental one the bisect review already documents), `task-025`+`vp-02-sprite-animation`+`tape-01-run-tape` 42/42 both projects, plain 390px boot shows the hero and five townsfolk advancing frames with zero console/page errors.
